  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the western edge of the Var department, Bandol Dog Beach is one of the few beaches in this area designed entirely for dogs. A small pebble cove on the Corniche Bonaparte, just below the Deferrari stadium and facing Bendor island, where dogs can swim freely under their owner's eye. "Toutounet" poop-bag dispensers are available year-round.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This is a compact spot — don't confuse it with the town's larger beaches. Important note for 2026: the stadium's historic car park closed permanently on 5 October 2025, replaced by a free temporary car park (5 free hours per day per vehicle) on the northern, street-facing half of the stadium — but the site is under construction for a future landscaped park, with possible temporary closures during the works. Check the Bandol town hall's latest updates before heading over.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if the Dog Beach feels too crowded, the one in nearby Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer is a good alternative.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Bandol's town centre, with its harbour and café terraces, is just a few minutes' walk away — handy for extending the outing.</p>
    </div>

